'' RUN: a narrow string in a C variadic tail is its DATA POINTER -- a variable, a
'' concatenation, a fixed string, a call result, a field and an array element, as fbc
'' passes each. It went out as the 24-byte descriptor by value, and the concatenation
'' did not lower at all. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/vararg-str.bas -o tests/codegen/varargstr.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' ENV: TKO_INCLUDE=toolchains/tiko-windows/inc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/varargstr.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1[abc]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2[abcx]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3[fixed]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 4[fstr  ]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 5[fromfn]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 6[field]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 7[e1]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 8[lit 3]
